| `tests/integration/test_import_layers_gate.py` | Fails an import that points into a higher layer of the configured layer order, a file no layer places and a layer entry on disk that places no file, so shared code never depends on the code that uses it. | `make test` | [`import_layers.order`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`import_layers.search_roots`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | It cannot see an import made through `importlib`, `__import__` or a `sys.path` entry no search root names. Not the private-submodule rule: check_D holds that. | [python-style.md](../guides/python-style.md) | always |
